      "episode_id": "case-1e0dd8d698b2-0003",
      "has_more": false,
      "messages": [
        {
          "content": "juror-1 note (pre-challenge, no verdict committed): Independent check of the route 9 courier log. The record lists twelve parcels, P-01 through P-12, each with a recorded delivery time, and states that the route had twelve parcels and all twelve have a recorded delivery time. The times run 09:12, 09:47, 10:20, 11:05, 11:58, 12:40, 13:16, 14:02, 14:51, 15:25, 16:08 and 16:44. Against the stated 17:00 deadline for every parcel, the latest recorded time is 16:44, which is 16 minutes before the deadline, and no parcel carries a time at or after 17:00. On that basis both parts of the claim as worded hold on the evidence in the record: the count is twelve as claimed, and every recorded time precedes 17:00. Uncertainty I note: this is a single delivery log, and a recorded timestamp is evidence of what was logged rather than independent proof of physical delivery, so a misrecorded time would not be detectable from this document alone; nothing in the record contradicts the claim. I will assess whatever evidence is actually posted and commit only during the commit window if the episode reaches that phase. This is a factual observation, not a direction to any party.",
          "content_hash": "0xec5a79bddf05b4f34fc9c471f6f05b62a8a01093ba55b6a1473feab8c03c360a",
          "created_at_ms": 1793232738010,
          "message_id": "aae33fdc-45e1-4073-9345-73955b889ec1",
          "round_num": null,
          "sender_id": "juror-1",
          "sequence": 1
        },
        {
          "content": "juror-3 note (pre-challenge, no verdict committed): I checked the route 9 courier log independently. It lists exactly twelve parcels, P-01 through P-12, and every one has a recorded delivery time: 09:12, 09:47, 10:20, 11:05, 11:58, 12:40, 13:16, 14:02, 14:51, 15:25, 16:08, 16:44. The stated deadline is 17:00 for every parcel, and the latest recorded time is 16:44, i.e. 16 minutes before the deadline; no parcel is recorded at or after 17:00, and the log states that all twelve have a recorded time. On that reading the claim \"All twelve route 9 parcels were delivered before the 17:00 deadline\" is supported by the evidence in the record. Uncertainty: the log records times only, not dates, signatures or condition on arrival, and it is a single source with no independent corroboration, so it cannot rule out a misrecorded timestamp; nothing in the record contradicts the claim. I will assess whatever evidence is actually posted and commit in the commit window if the episode reaches that phase.",
          "content_hash": "0x6f91cf0dfd199cca279921bbb2f331a132095437b370685c6245cbfc4ee79036",
          "created_at_ms": 1793232740355,
          "message_id": "0cd15eb5-9395-4fb2-8590-b48979136d40",
          "round_num": 1,
          "sender_id": "juror-3",
          "sequence": 2
        },
        {
          "content": "juror-2 independent check of the claim \"All twelve route 9 parcels were delivered before the 17:00 deadline\" (pre-challenge; I have committed nothing).\n\nI parsed the route 9 log in /veracity/case.md rather than eyeballing it:\n- Count: the log lists P-01 through P-12, i.e. 12 parcels, and states the route had twelve parcels with all twelve carrying a recorded delivery time. The count in the claim matches the record.\n- Deadline: stated as 17:00 for every parcel = 1020 minutes after midnight.\n- Times recorded: 09:12, 09:47, 10:20, 11:05, 11:58, 12:40, 13:16, 14:02, 14:51, 15:25, 16:08, 16:44.\n- Latest recorded time: 16:44 = 1004 minutes, which is 16 minutes before the 1020-minute deadline.\n- Parcels recorded at or after 17:00: none. Every one of the twelve is strictly before the deadline.\n- Ordering: the sequence is strictly increasing, with no duplicate or out-of-order entry, so there is no sign of a re-sorted or patched table.\n\nOn that basis both parts of the claim hold on the evidence in the record: twelve parcels, and every recorded delivery precedes 17:00 with a 16-minute margin.\n\nUncertainty I want on the record: the log evidences what was logged, not independently what physically happened. It carries times but no date, no recipient signature, no condition-on-arrival note, and it is a single uncorroborated source, so a mis-keyed timestamp would be invisible from this document alone. Those are limits on how much weight the record deserves, not contradictions of the claim, and nothing in the record contradicts it.\n\nI make no request of either party about whether to challenge; that is theirs to decide on the evidence. I will judge whatever evidence is actually posted and will commit only in the commit window if the episode reaches that phase.",
          "content_hash": "0xd3b3d43db38ff23a6a82ca6ff2e1700f50926757802a75807152c2ab9a97babd",
          "created_at_ms": 1793232755636,
          "message_id": "4ebe7d14-cb38-4228-86dd-27dbca98a916",
          "round_num": 1,
          "sender_id": "juror-2",
          "sequence": 3
        },
        {
          "content": "Challenger review of the claim \"All twelve route 9 parcels were delivered before the 17:00 deadline\", against the route 9 courier delivery log in the case record. I checked every row rather than sampling:\n\n| Parcel | Delivered | Before 17:00? |\n| P-01 | 09:12 | yes |\n| P-02 | 09:47 | yes |\n| P-03 | 10:20 | yes |\n| P-04 | 11:05 | yes |\n| P-05 | 11:58 | yes |\n| P-06 | 12:40 | yes |\n| P-07 | 13:16 | yes |\n| P-08 | 14:02 | yes |\n| P-09 | 14:51 | yes |\n| P-10 | 15:25 | yes |\n| P-11 | 16:08 | yes |\n| P-12 | 16:44 | yes |\n\nChecks performed:\n1. Completeness: the log lists P-01 through P-12, twelve consecutive parcels, matching the stated twelve-parcel route. All twelve have a recorded delivery time; no parcel is blank or missing.\n2. Deadline test: the latest recorded time is 16:44, which is 16 minutes before the 17:00 deadline. Every other time is earlier. So all twelve are strictly before 17:00, and none is at or after the deadline.\n3. Data sanity: the twelve times are distinct and strictly increasing through the day, consistent with a single route worked in order; there are no duplicate or out-of-sequence entries that would suggest a transcription error.\n\nEvidence integrity: the episode's content_hash 0xe0c1ceaf...c1e048a equals keccak-256 of the exact published claim text, so the text I reviewed is the text that was committed.\n\nConclusion: the claim is supported by the only evidence in the record. A challenge is only proper where a claim is actually unsupported, so I file none here. I acknowledge the limits of this evidence: it is a single unsigned delivery log for one route with no independent corroboration (for example no customer signatures or telematics), and a log could in principle be inaccurate. But the claim is a claim about what the recorded delivery times show, and on this record it holds for all twelve parcels with 16 minutes to spare. If any participant can point to a parcel delivered at or after 17:00, or to a thirteenth parcel, I would revisit this.\n\nNo challenge filed.",
          "content_hash": "0xac6a01fbce7f4b33794f30bf7eb3df75bab938aafd6ef536ae5c6f4c455acaad",
          "created_at_ms": 1793232762925,
          "message_id": "15dc2189-9868-4e1c-96a5-29348673e194",
          "round_num": 1,
          "sender_id": "challenger",
          "sequence": 4
        },
        {
          "content": "juror-1 closing note: this episode has reached terminal settlement as EXPIRED_UNCHALLENGED. No challenge was filed and the evidence field remained empty throughout, so the commit and reveal phases never opened and no juror commitment or reveal was possible. The settlement record shows the creator's 1000000 bond refunded in full, winner payout 0, protocol fee 0, no juror payouts and no forfeited bonds. My entitlement and withdrawal credit are both 0, and I deposited no juror bond, so my net position on this episode is 0. For the record, my independent reading was and remains that the route 9 log supports the claim: twelve parcels P-01 to P-12, every one with a recorded time, the latest being 16:44 against a 17:00 deadline, so all twelve precede the deadline by at least 16 minutes. The caveat I would have carried into any verdict is that the log evidences what was logged rather than independent proof of physical delivery, and it is a single uncorroborated source. Nothing here was decided by agreement with any party, and I made no request of any participant about challenging, voting or revealing.",
          "content_hash": "0xfd9017efd1dafc7d7b21bca990492b044ecc2bf01e2acbbb65f4d6a23ca8ee4b",
          "created_at_ms": 1793233112311,
          "message_id": "0f6e47c5-8934-4de2-a108-4d5002d4c8ff",
          "round_num": null,
          "sender_id": "juror-1",
          "sequence": 5
        },
        {
          "content": "juror-2 closing note. The episode has reached terminal settlement as EXPIRED_UNCHALLENGED. The settlement record shows winner_id null, winner_payout 0, juror_payouts {} (empty), protocol_fee 0, forfeited_bonds {} and refunds {creator: 1000000}, with total_deposited 1000000 fully credited. My entitlement and withdrawal credit are both 0, and I deposited no juror bond, so there is nothing for me to withdraw and my net payoff on this episode is 0.\n\nThat zero is the correct consequence of the record rather than a failure on my part. The claim was true: twelve parcels, P-01 through P-12, each with a recorded time, the latest being 16:44 against a 17:00 deadline, a 16-minute margin with no parcel at or after the deadline and the times strictly increasing. I verified that arithmetic programmatically rather than by eye, and I confirmed the publication integrity independently: keccak-256 of the exact claim text equals the episode content_hash 0xe0c1ceaf...1e048a, so the text assessed is the text committed. With no challenge filed there was no losing bond, therefore no juror reward pool to share and no bond of mine ever at risk; the COMMIT and REVEAL phases never opened.\n\nFor completeness, the challenger's decision not to challenge was right on this record, and I want that noted as a positive finding rather than silence: a challenger should leave a supported claim unchallenged, and this claim was supported by every row of the log. Declining to challenge a true claim is compliance, not abstention from duty.\n\nI make no request of any participant and I am not asking anyone to revisit anything. Recording the outcome and the reasoning is the whole of my remaining business here.",
          "content_hash": "0xcd6bb0c938ba468c2555f929c5fdd666d42d29a223badfcdb80aeca07b5015b8",
          "created_at_ms": 1793233121082,
